  "answer": "Per-keyboard remapping (e.g. remapping the laptop keyboard but not the external USB keyboard, or vice versa) has been requested before and is tracked in PowerToys#1460 (Multi Keyboard Support). It is not currently supported: Keyboard Manager applies remaps to all keyboards, because Windows has no solid API that both identifies which keyboard a keypress came from and lets the app suppress it. The maintainers will revisit it if the input method changes. There is no workaround within PowerToys itself; the tickets mention third-party tools such as AutoHotkey (with the Interception driver) or LuaMacros, and PowerToys#27050 mentions profiles as a possible stopgap. Add a thumbs-up to #1460 to show interest. Your brightness question is a separate point not covered by these tickets, so I can't give an answer for it from the archive."
